  "issue_title": "Harden offline substance scoring beyond title/theme presence",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n#69 corrected the offline stand-in judge so it ranks submissions by *substance* rather than plan length (#54). The current substance signal keys on the presence of `title`/`theme` fields \u2014 a good start, but still gameable: a plan can score by stuffing generic titles/themes with no concrete, actionable content.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Count concrete action fields beyond `title`/`theme` (e.g. `kind`, `files`, `rationale`) where the plan schema supports them\n- [ ] Downrank generic filler titles rather than reward mere field presence\n- [ ] Add a judge-robustness test: a padded/filler plan must not outrank a substantive shorter one (verified from both pairwise positions)\n- [ ] Keep the offline path fully deterministic (no network)\n\n## Pointers\n`benchmark/score.py` (offline substance heuristic), `tests/test_score.py`. Follows from #69 / #54.\n",
